# Dungeon Dockerfile Procedure

## Overview

This document explains the Docker build and hardening procedure used for the `Dungeon` microservice.

The objective is to provide a Docker image that is:

- Secure
- Optimized
- Production-ready
- Easy to maintain
- Compatible with CI/CD pipelines
- Efficient regarding Docker layer caching
- Executed with a non-root user
- Free from unnecessary SDK and source files at runtime

The Dockerfile uses a multi-stage build strategy with dedicated stages for:

1. Dependency restoration
2. Application build
3. Automated tests
4. Application publishing
5. Production runtime

---

# Project Structure

The `Dungeon` solution contains the following projects:

```text
Dungeon.Presentation.slnx

Dungeon.Contracts/
├── Dungeon.Contracts.csproj

Dungeon.Domain/
├── Dungeon.Domain.csproj

Dungeon.Application/
├── Dungeon.Application.csproj

Dungeon.Infrastructure/
├── Dungeon.Infrastructure.csproj

Dungeon.Presentation/
├── Dungeon.Presentation.csproj

Dungeon.Test/
├── Dungeon.Test.csproj
```

The `Dungeon.Presentation` project is the ASP.NET Core entry point of the microservice.

---

# Dockerfile

```dockerfile
# syntax=docker/dockerfile:1.7

ARG DOTNET_VERSION=10.0

# ============================================================
# 1. RESTORE
# ============================================================
FROM mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/sdk:${DOTNET_VERSION} AS restore

WORKDIR /src

# Copy only project files first to maximize Docker cache usage.
COPY Dungeon.Presentation.slnx ./

COPY Dungeon.Contracts/Dungeon.Contracts.csproj \
     Dungeon.Contracts/

COPY Dungeon.Domain/Dungeon.Domain.csproj \
     Dungeon.Domain/

COPY Dungeon.Application/Dungeon.Application.csproj \
     Dungeon.Application/

COPY Dungeon.Infrastructure/Dungeon.Infrastructure.csproj \
     Dungeon.Infrastructure/

COPY Dungeon.Presentation/Dungeon.Presentation.csproj \
     Dungeon.Presentation/

COPY Dungeon.Test/Dungeon.Test.csproj \
     Dungeon.Test/

# Restore NuGet dependencies using the BuildKit cache.
RUN --mount=type=cache,target=/root/.nuget/packages \
    dotnet restore Dungeon.Presentation.slnx


# ============================================================
# 2. BUILD
# ============================================================
FROM restore AS build

COPY . .

RUN --mount=type=cache,target=/root/.nuget/packages \
    dotnet build Dungeon.Presentation.slnx \
    --configuration Release \
    --no-restore


# ============================================================
# 3. TEST
# ============================================================
FROM build AS test

RUN --mount=type=cache,target=/root/.nuget/packages \
    dotnet test Dungeon.Test/Dungeon.Test.csproj \
    --configuration Release \
    --no-build \
    --verbosity normal \
    --logger "console;verbosity=normal"


# ============================================================
# 4. PUBLISH
# ============================================================
FROM build AS publish

RUN --mount=type=cache,target=/root/.nuget/packages \
    dotnet publish Dungeon.Presentation/Dungeon.Presentation.csproj \
    --configuration Release \
    --output /app/publish \
    --no-build \
    --no-restore \
    /p:UseAppHost=false


# ============================================================
# 5. RUNTIME
# ============================================================
FROM mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/aspnet:${DOTNET_VERSION} AS runtime

WORKDIR /app

ENV ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Production \
    ASPNETCORE_HTTP_PORTS=8080 \
    DOTNET_RUNNING_IN_CONTAINER=true \
    DOTNET_EnableDiagnostics=0

EXPOSE 8080

COPY --from=publish --chown=$APP_UID:$APP_UID /app/publish ./

USER $APP_UID

ENTRYPOINT ["dotnet", "Dungeon.Presentation.dll"]
```

