# CI/CD Example

A basic CI/CD Docker workflow can follow this sequence:

```text
Source Code
    |
    v
Docker Test Stage
    |
    v
Automated Tests
    |
    v
Production Image Build
    |
    v
Security Scan
    |
    v
Container Registry
    |
    v
Deployment
```

Example commands:

```bash
docker build --target test -t dungeon-test .
```

Then:

```bash
docker build -t dungeon-api:${VERSION} .
```

The resulting image can then be pushed to a container registry.

Example:

```bash
docker tag \
    dungeon-api:${VERSION} \
    registry.example.com/dungeon-api:${VERSION}
```

```bash
docker push \
    registry.example.com/dungeon-api:${VERSION}
```

