# Recommended Production Improvements

Additional security controls can be added around the Docker image.

## Pin Docker Images

For stronger supply-chain security, base images can be pinned using their SHA-256 digest.

Conceptual example:

```dockerfile
FROM mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/aspnet:10.0@sha256:<IMAGE_DIGEST>
```

This guarantees that the exact expected base image is used.

The digest must be updated intentionally when upgrading the base image.

---

## Scan the Image

The production image should be scanned for known vulnerabilities.

Examples of tools that can be integrated into CI/CD include:

```text
Docker Scout
Trivy
Grype
Snyk
Microsoft Defender for Containers
```

---

## Do Not Use `latest` in Production

For development, this is acceptable:

```text
dungeon-api:latest
```

For production, immutable version tags should preferably be used.

Example:

```text
dungeon-api:1.4.2
```

or:

```text
dungeon-api:git-a84f91c
```

This makes deployments easier to track and rollback.

