# Summary

The hardened `Dungeon` Dockerfile provides:

- Multi-stage Docker builds
- Docker BuildKit NuGet caching
- Isolated automated testing
- Release builds
- Optimized publishing
- Minimal production runtime
- Non-root execution
- Explicit production configuration
- Disabled .NET diagnostics
- Reduced attack surface
- No SDK in the production image
- No source code in the production image
- No test project in the production image
- Better CI/CD compatibility
- Better Docker layer caching
- Optional chiseled runtime support

This Dockerfile structure should be reused across the different .NET microservices to maintain a consistent container security baseline.
